Rarely have I won two games so close together, but the dwarven
archaeologist I ascended on Christmas Day I had actually started
playing over a year before. Ascending gave me the desire to renew my
quest to win with all of the races, having already won with all of the
character classes. (I don't think I'm going to try to win with all
possible combos of race and class, however.)

So I chose the humble orc, and feeling in a destructive hack-and-slash
mood (hence Shiva, the destroyer), the Barbarian class. Many think this
is one of the easier classes to play, and I did breeze through this
game relatively easily. Having lots of altars helped, but the main
bonus was my cat stepping on a polymorph trap early in the game and
becoming a baby blue dragon. She quickly matured and ate all of the
shopkeepers in Minetown and elsewhere, enabling me to buy protection
easily early on. She also nicely took out Juiblex early for me when I
accidentally summoned him at an altar in the main dungeon (not used to
playing an orc!)

I was worried I wouldn't get a good weapon being a chaotic (I don't
like Stormbringer's risks), so I was fortunate that Set granted me
Frost Brand. I tried dual-weaponing with a silver saber for awhile, but
ended up going for the added AC of a shield of reflection (plus
homemade gray dragon scale).

The hardest thing was finding a bag of holding, or indeed a sack of any
kind. I was quite deep in the dungeon, nearly at the Medusa level,
before I got one (Sokoban had an amulet of reflection, which did prove
useful until I got the shield).

The next hardest thing was finding the stairs to Vlad's Tower, which
had never been a problem before. I ended up going up and down many
levels of Gehennom repeatedly, stopping at the Orcus town altar
frequently and gaining lots of HP from nurses along the way. When I
finally did find and take out Vlad, I spent quite a long time in the
tower, hopping off and on the magic trap on the first level, boosting
my charisma to the max (useful for incubus encounters) and getting lots
of polypile fodder and blankable scrolls for the four magic markers I'd
found.

Not intending to keep any conducts in this particular game, I genocided
h (after getting mind-flayed three times) ;L and disenchanters, and
used several wishes, though not for any artifacts (got impatient trying
to polypile speed boots, among other things; I didn't find a wand of
polymorph till long past Fort Ludios). My last wish, right before the
end game, was for a ring of slow digestion (also never encountered or
polypiled in the game), as I didn't want to worry about eating when
facing Famine etc.

Endgame was very easy; cursed/confused gold detection found the
portals, no annoying Archons bothered me on Air (a couple did visit
Vlad's Tower), and never had to deal with Pestilence. Famine was no
problem given the ring of slow digestion, and Death drained off some
max HP but I still ended with over 500.

